    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the dimly lit command center of Orbital Station Aether-7, a top-secret research facility orbiting a gas giant. The warning klaxons are blaring a rhythmic pulse, signaling that the station's structural integrity is rapidly deteriorating after a massive micro-meteoroid impact. The automated systems are offline, and the primary AI has entered a hard lockdown, severing all communication arrays. Your only chance of survival is to manually bypass the security overrides and send a distress signal to the planetary fleet stationed on the moon below. The control room is littered with offline equipment, locked biometric safes, and experimental tech components scattered across the floor. You must navigate through the station's archaic data protocols, reactivate the necessary encryption modules, and broadcast your precise coordinates before the hull breaches completely and the oxygen runs out. Every second counts as the metal groans around you.",
